Remove the Google/Vertex provider family (PATCH_OUT_GOOGLE_PROVIDER, default 1).

Two cuts in vendored charm.land/fantasy (Crush itself is untouched):
1. providers/google is gutted to a stub (google_removed.go): the genai-backed
   implementation is deleted, un-compiling google.golang.org/genai,
   cloud.google.com/go/{auth,civil,compute/metadata}, gorilla/websocket and
   the OTel instrumentation. provider_options.go (metadata types, no genai
   dependency) is kept so the openrouter/vercel hooks and Crush compile.
2. providers/anthropic loses its Vertex branch (anthropic-sdk-go/vertex +
   golang.org/x/oauth2/google imports), un-compiling google.golang.org/api,
   grpc, s2a-go, gax-go, oauth2adapt and the GCE metadata probe; a
   Vertex-configured provider fails with an explicit error.
Import lines are REPLACED by unique marker comments (never bare-deleted) so
every hunk is anchored in both directions; zero-context hunks are used where
no-bedrock-aws.patch edits the same lines. Apply with git apply --unidiff-zero.
See tasks/reference/dependency-network-audit.md section 4.1 and D5.

